# SemText npl-cot — chain-of-thought disclosure, both display modes
# Direction A "Slate Console". Two example panels in one frame: the expanded
# (default) state and the `collapsed` state, so the disclosure semantics and
# the outcome-stays-visible invariant are both readable at a glance.
#
# MODE 1 — expanded (default, `collapsed` absent):
#   visible: the disclosure summary row (chevron pointing DOWN + a step-count
#     chip) and the numbered reasoning-step rows beneath it, then the outcome
#     block at the foot of the panel.
#   must never: hide the steps while open; reorder the outcome above the steps;
#     add a second summary row.
# MODE 2 — collapsed (`<npl-cot collapsed>`):
#   visible: the same summary row with the chevron pointing RIGHT, the step
#     area compacted away, and the outcome block STILL present and fully
#     readable at the foot — this is the invariant (the answer stays visible
#     while the reasoning is folded).
#   must never: drop or dim the outcome; reveal any step row; turn the toggle
#     into a custom button (it is a native details/summary affordance).
#
# Reference snapshots are produced by the snapshot-harness lane
# (`npm run snap:tag -- npl-cot`, output into
# .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-cot/). Attach the best `-render-`
# PNGs from that directory before generation; the attachments block below is
# left commented out because the harness was not yet available when this
# prompt was written (see reports/tag-npl-cot.md).
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-cot
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of two side-by-side reference-page panels illustrating
    one disclosure element in its two display states, wide 16:9, flat
    technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D). Dark slate navy
    background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and a faint violet
    radial glow upper-left. Two equal panels sit side by side, separated by a
    thin slate hairline divider, each panel a dark slate card (#1E293B) with a
    thin slate hairline border, squared corners, deep soft shadow; a small
    dim caption bar sits above each panel.

    Left panel — EXPANDED (the default state). Top row: a disclosure summary
    row made of a small violet (#7C3AED) chevron pointing DOWN, a wide pale
    placeholder bar for the summary label, and a small soft-violet (#A78BFA)
    rounded chip holding three tiny dots (an abstract step count, never
    digits). Beneath it, three stacked step rows separated by 1px slate
    hairlines: each row has a thin vertical violet (#7C3AED) rule on its left
    edge, a small solid soft-violet bullet, and one or two muted slate
    placeholder bars of varying length. At the foot of the panel, set apart by
    a slightly wider gap and a soft-violet tinted fill (#312E81 at low
    opacity) with a violet left edge accent, the outcome block: two brighter
    near-white placeholder bars, clearly more prominent than the step bars.

    Right panel — COLLAPSED (the `collapsed` state). Identical summary row at
    the top, except the chevron points RIGHT, signalling folded. The step area
    beneath it is empty — the three step rows and their violet rules are gone,
    leaving compact clean space. At the foot of the panel the outcome block is
    UNCHANGED: the same soft-violet tinted fill, violet left edge accent and
    two bright bars, still fully visible and readable. The two panels' outcome
    blocks must be pixel-comparable, the only difference between panels being
    the chevron direction and the presence or absence of the step rows. All
    copy is abstract placeholder bars — strictly no letters, digits, or words
    anywhere.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, light mode, white cards, rounded corners,
    3D, photorealism, faces, avatars, robot mascots, more than two panels,
    a second summary row, a hidden or dimmed outcome block, a visible step row
    in the collapsed panel, checkbox or blur-out occlusion overlays
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette, two-panel state comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

# attachments:
#   - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-cot/npl-cot-expanded-render-1280.png
#     role: reference
#     description: expanded state — summary row, step rows, outcome at foot
#   - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-cot/npl-cot-collapsed-render-1280.png
#     role: reference
#     description: collapsed state — chevron folded right, outcome still visible

requirements:
  subject: two panels of one chain-of-thought block — left expanded with three
    numbered-rule step rows plus an outcome block, right collapsed with the
    step rows removed and the identical outcome block still visible
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet
    chevron and rules, one soft-violet outcome fill
  composition: two equal panels side by side, consistent summary row height,
    outcome blocks aligned at the same baseline in both panels
  do:
    - keep the outcome block visually identical in both panels
    - make the collapsed panel's step area clearly empty
    - differentiate the summary chevron by direction only (down vs right)
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, or logos
    - a missing, dimmed, or occluded outcome in the collapsed panel
    - a step row visible in the collapsed panel

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - disclosure_semantics
    - outcome_invariant
  criteria:
    disclosure_semantics:
      weight: 3
      description: Left panel shows an opened disclosure (chevron down, step
        rows present); right panel shows it closed (chevron right, step rows
        absent)
      fail_signals:
        - both chevrons point the same way
        - step rows visible in the collapsed panel
        - toggle drawn as a button rather than a disclosure row
    outcome_invariant:
      weight: 3
      description: The outcome block is present, equally prominent and
        readable in both panels
      fail_signals:
        - outcome missing or dimmed when collapsed
        - outcome sits inside the folded area
        - outcome styled differently between panels
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 2
      description: Dark slate + violet, squared hairline panels, flat style
      fail_signals:
        - light theme
        - glossy 3D look
        - rounded corners
  reject_if:
    - any legible text, letters, digits, words, watermark, or logo
    - a hidden, dimmed, or absent outcome block in the collapsed panel
    - more than two panels or a chaotic layout

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-cot